ഒന്നാം ഘട്ടത്തിലെ പരിശോധന.

Hamlet, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Cordelia, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Desdemona, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Portia, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Miranda, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Falstaff, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Rosalind, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: കണക്കിന്റെ പ്രധാന ഘട്ടം.

Scene I: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Enter Prospero and Hamlet]
Prospero: You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Juliet]
Prospero: You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Romeo]
Prospero: You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Othello]
Prospero: You are a big hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Macbeth]
Prospero: You are a big hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Enter Prospero and Lady Macbeth]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big big big big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of the sum of a big big big big hero and a big big big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big big big big big hero and the sum of a big big big hero and the sum of a big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Desdemona]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big big big big big big hero and the sum of a big big hero and the sum of a big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Portia]
Prospero: You are as good as the sum of a big big big big big big hero and the sum of a big big big big big hero and the sum of a big big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Act II: കണക്കിന്റെ പ്രധാന ഘട്ടം.

Scene I: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Enter Prospero and Falstaff]
Prospero: You are a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Rosalind]
Prospero: You are as good as the difference between a big big big big big big big hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Falstaff and Rosalind]

Scene II: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
Falstaff: Are you better than nothing?
Rosalind:
 If not, let us proceed to scene III.
Falstaff: You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
Rosalind:
 You are as good as the product of yourself and a big hero.
 Let us return to scene II.

Scene III: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Prospero and Falstaff]
Prospero: You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Act III: കണക്കിന്റെ പ്രധാന ഘട്ടം.

Scene I: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Enter Prospero and Miranda]
Prospero:
 You are as good as Hamlet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big hero and a hero and Juliet.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of a big big hero and Romeo.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and Othello.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and the product of a big big big hero and Macbeth.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Lady Macbeth.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Ophelia.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Cordelia.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Desdemona.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Portia.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Falstaff.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

Act IV: കണക്കിന്റെ പ്രധാന ഘട്ടം.

Scene I: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.
[Enter Prospero and Miranda]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of the product of Miranda and Miranda and the product of the sum of a big hero and a hero and Miranda.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and Lady Macbeth.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Falstaff.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
